# Derived from deploy/.env for compose.services.yaml: not settings to edit. Each bundled service runs unless deploy/.env
# names one of your own: the database with DB_HOST, the media storage with S3_UPLOADS_BUCKET_NAME. Each value is 0 then, and
# empty otherwise, which compose.services.yaml reads as 1: the scale of the postgres and storage services, which also tells
# the backend services which they use. Compose reads these settings from the shell's environment before deploy/.env, so a
# DB_HOST or S3_UPLOADS_BUCKET_NAME exported in the shell that runs docker compose chooses as well.
LUMI_BUNDLED_DATABASE=${DB_HOST:+0}
LUMI_BUNDLED_STORAGE=${S3_UPLOADS_BUCKET_NAME:+0}
